=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
  play firewall/profiles ---------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode: hardn's own screens and prompts, on the real$
# plan/apply engine against a simulated host, hostfake's$
# recording host.System, whose commands a model of the host$
# answers. Nothing on this machine changes: every command and$
# file is the fake's, and its record is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: firewall/profiles$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. ufw active on 22, hardn.yml$
# with two application profiles, not applied.$
$
# UFW Firewall Configuration ###################################$
$
  [+] Firewall             Configured deny policy$
$
  ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [+] Status               Active$
  [+] Incoming policy      Deny$
  [+] At boot              Yes$
$
  SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] [::]:22              Allowed$
  [+] 0.0.0.0:22           Allowed$
$
  Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] 22/tcp               Allow$
  [+] 22/tcp (v6)          Allow$
$
  Application Profiles -----------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] LabHTTPS             30443/tcp Not applied$
  [ ] LabDNS               8853/tcp Not applied$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disable firewall     Stop ufw (not recommended)$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
   3) Trusted Interfaces   Add, remove, apply$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-3 or q]: 2$
$
# Manage UFW Application Profiles ##############################$
$
  Application Profiles -----------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] LabHTTPS             30443/tcp Not applied$
  [ ] LabDNS               8853/tcp Not applied$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Add profile          Save a profile in hardn.yml$
   2) Remove profile       Take one out of hardn.yml$
   3) Apply profiles       Let their ports through ufw$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-3 or q]: 2$
$
# Remove Profile ###############################################$
$
  Remove which profile?$
$
   1) LabHTTPS$
   2) LabDNS$
$
    > Option [1-2, 0 or q]: 1$
  Remove which profile?: LabHTTPS$
$
# Warning$
# This takes the profile out of hardn.yml. A rule already in ufw$
# stays.$
$
   -  Save the configuration$
      /etc/hardn/hardn.yml$
      @@ -1,11 +1,6 @@$
       # hardn's configuration (web-01.example.net)$
       username: alice$
       ufwAppProfiles:$
      -  - name: LabHTTPS$
      -    title: Lab Web Server (HTTPS)$
      -    description: Lab Web server secure port$
      -    ports:$
      -      - "30443/tcp"$
         - name: LabDNS$
           title: Lab DNS$
           description: Lab DNS over TLS$
$
  Remove LabHTTPS? [y/N, 0 or q]: y$
$
  [+] Save the configuration  Done$
$
# Operation Successful$
$
  Backup of /etc/hardn/hardn.yml kept in$
  /var/backups/hardn/20261020T120000Z-xxxxxxxx$
$
# Manage UFW Application Profiles ##############################$
$
  Application Profiles -----------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] LabDNS               8853/tcp Not applied$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Add profile          Save a profile in hardn.yml$
   2) Remove profile       Take one out of hardn.yml$
   3) Apply profiles       Let their ports through ufw$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-3 or q]: 0$
$
# UFW Firewall Configuration ###################################$
$
  [+] Firewall             Configured deny policy$
$
  ufw ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Installed            Yes$
  [+] Status               Active$
  [+] Incoming policy      Deny$
  [+] At boot              Yes$
$
  SSH ----------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] [::]:22              Allowed$
  [+] 0.0.0.0:22           Allowed$
$
  Rules --------------------------------------------------------$
$
  [+] 22/tcp               Allow$
  [+] 22/tcp (v6)          Allow$
$
  Application Profiles -----------------------------------------$
$
  [ ] LabDNS               8853/tcp Not applied$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Disable firewall     Stop ufw (not recommended)$
   2) Application Profiles Add, remove, apply$
   3) Trusted Interfaces   Add, remove, apply$
$
   0) Return$
$
    > Option [0-3 or q]: 0$
$
  simulated system ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Info: firewall/profiles$
# Recorded by the fake, not done: what each step ran on$
# web-01.example.net, and the files it changed, in order;$
# hardn's own journal, run directory and backups left out.$
$
   -  Applied: Save the configuration$
      /etc/hardn/hardn.yml$
$

